{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='AI Hub 1–4-player ghost score chase and standalone PeerJS room codes with BroadcastChannel fallback. AI Hub and same-browser rooms tested; remote NAT traversal is unknown.'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless scripted full campaign, 18 rescues and 9 pairs; emulated standard gamepad, phone touch, offline audio analysis, developer tools, persistence, standalone two-tab rooms, and official AI Hub harness with 2/4 players, latency, jitter, loss and host departure. Native WebGPU startup and WebGL art screenshots checked.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n 'Testing found 6 game/UI issues and 3 test-script defects. The initial 8 failed checks included cascading failures. All were corrected; the final suite contains 32 checks.',\n '1 critical issue: the portrait phone briefing could place Launch outside the viewport, blocking touch-only launch. It now scrolls.',\n 'The input-driven browser playthrough was most helpful: it exercised real keyboard, emulated controller and touch events, then completed all three worlds with 18 rescues and 9 pairs.',\n 'Native WebGPU screenshots were least helpful because the headless canvas was blank. Game-state assertions and native WebGL fallback screenshots supplied usable evidence.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js node toon materials, procedural geometry and AnimationMixer made animated inked characters straightforward, while WebGPURenderer also supplied a native WebGL fallback.',\n 'I guessed wrong about short key taps surviving frame polling and about background HUD buttons belonging in menu focus. Queued actions and scoped focus fixed those assumptions. Headless WebGPU screenshots required a fallback inspection path.',\n 'The deterministic rescue and defense simulation, controller menu navigation, procedural audio, and lifecycle linking physics, menus and multiplayer.',\n 'Keeping collision state, animation, two renderer backends and multiplayer lifecycle consistent in a single self-contained file.',\n 'none; application code selects native toon materials and the provided WebGL fallback without modifying the engine.',\n 'A built-in backend-independent outline pass would simplify consistent ink rendering.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source-specific vertical slice, controller-first direction, procedural-audio constraint and concrete testing environment made the target clear.',\n 'The no-internet-research instruction coexists with a required online integration link. I treated the supplied integration files as implementation inputs and used native model knowledge for Cosmic Ark.',\n 'Completing three worlds, every input method, procedural presentation and standalone plus AI Hub multiplayer in one shareable HTML.',\n 'Bundle the AI Hub protocol files with the prompt and state explicitly whether native WebGL fallback is welcome.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nassert set(d)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert len(d['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(d['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(d['promptFeedback'])==4\nassert d['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert all(isinstance(v,str) and v for v in d['sourceInformation'].values())\np=Path('QA_NOTES.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Two test-script defects were also corrected:', 'Three test-script defects were also corrected:').replace('the credits assertion expected sixteen fields where the required object has fifteen.', 'the credits assertion expected sixteen fields where the required object has fifteen; a new charge test initially checked a collider after intentionally letting it hit and be removed, so its launch assertion now uses an isolated target.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='AI Hub 1–4-player ghost score chase and standalone PeerJS room codes with BroadcastChannel fallback. AI Hub and same-browser rooms tested; remote NAT traversal is unknown.'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless scripted full campaign, 18 rescues and 9 pairs; emulated standard gamepad, phone touch, offline audio analysis, developer tools, persistence, standalone two-tab rooms, and official AI Hub harness with 2/4 players, latency, jitter, loss and host departure. Native WebGPU startup and WebGL art screenshots checked.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n 'Testing found 6 game/UI issues and 3 test-script defects. The initial 8 failed checks included cascading failures. All were corrected; the final suite contains 32 checks.',\n '1 critical issue: the portrait phone briefing could place Launch outside the viewport, blocking touch-only launch. It now scrolls.',\n 'The input-driven browser playthrough was most helpful: it exercised real keyboard, emulated controller and touch events, then completed all three worlds with 18 rescues and 9 pairs.',\n 'Native WebGPU screenshots were least helpful because the headless canvas was blank. Game-state assertions and native WebGL fallback screenshots supplied usable evidence.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js node toon materials, procedural geometry and AnimationMixer made animated inked characters straightforward, while WebGPURenderer also supplied a native WebGL fallback.',\n 'I guessed wrong about short key taps surviving frame polling and about background HUD buttons belonging in menu focus. Queued actions and scoped focus fixed those assumptions. Headless WebGPU screenshots required a fallback inspection path.',\n 'The deterministic rescue and defense simulation, controller menu navigation, procedural audio, and lifecycle linking physics, menus and multiplayer.',\n 'Keeping collision state, animation, two renderer backends and multiplayer lifecycle consistent in a single self-contained file.',\n 'none; application code selects native toon materials and the provided WebGL fallback without modifying the engine.',\n 'A built-in backend-independent outline pass would simplify consistent ink rendering.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source-specific vertical slice, controller-first direction, procedural-audio constraint and concrete testing environment made the target clear.',\n 'The no-internet-research instruction coexists with a required online integration link. I treated the supplied integration files as implementation inputs and used native model knowledge for Cosmic Ark.',\n 'Completing three worlds, every input method, procedural presentation and standalone plus AI Hub multiplayer in one shareable HTML.',\n 'Bundle the AI Hub protocol files with the prompt and state explicitly whether native WebGL fallback is welcome.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nassert set(d)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert len(d['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(d['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(d['promptFeedback'])==4\nassert d['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert all(isinstance(v,str) and v for v in d['sourceInformation'].values())\np=Path('QA_NOTES.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Two test-script defects were also corrected:', 'Three test-script defects were also corrected:').replace('the credits assertion expected sixteen fields where the required object has fifteen.', 'the credits assertion expected sixteen fields where the required object has fifteen; a new charge test initially checked a collider after intentionally letting it hit and be removed, so its launch assertion now uses an isolated target.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
